!script {{
  --/| ==========================================================================
  --/| Tutorial: Writing Existing D&D 2024 Beacon Repeating Rows
  --/|
  --/| PURPOSE
  --/| This tutorial shows two ways to change a field on an existing Beacon
  --/| repeating row while keeping the familiar ScriptCards repeating commands.
  --/|
  --/| HOW TO USE IT
  --/| 1. Select a D&D 2024 Beacon NPC with at least one normal Action.
  --/| 2. Run this ScriptCard.
  --/| 3. The first Action is renamed temporarily in two different ways.
  --/| 4. The original name is restored after each test.
  --/|
  --/| CLASSIC SHEETS
  --/| On a classic sheet, a repeating row is made from Roll20 Attribute objects.
  --/| The !a command is therefore the natural command for a traditional
  --/| repeating attribute name such as:
  --/|
  --/| repeating_npcaction_ROWID_name
  --/|
  --/| BEACON SHEETS
  --/| Beacon stores Actions as native records, not classic repeating Attribute
  --/| rows. ScriptCards provides two useful ways to write an existing field.
  --/|
  --/| METHOD 1: !a COMPATIBILITY WRITE
  --/| You can build the familiar repeating_section_ROWID_field name and use !a.
  --/| ScriptCards finds the matching Beacon record and changes the real field
  --/| instead of creating a fake legacy repeating Attribute.
  --/|
  --/| METHOD 2: R WRITABLE TARGET WITH !c
  --/| When a repeating row is loaded, [*R>field] asks ScriptCards for a safe
  --/| writable path to that field in the Beacon record.
  --/|
  --/| Because the returned value is a structured Beacon path, write it with !c.
  --/|
  --/| IMPORTANT
  --/| Writable targets protect record identity fields such as the row ID,
  --/| shortID, and uuid. They are meant for ordinary editable fields.
  --/|
  --/| This tutorial changes an Action name only long enough to verify each write,
  --/| then restores the original name.
  --/| ==========================================================================

  --#beaconsheet|1
  --#sourcetoken|@{selected|token_id}
  --#title|[*S:npc_name] - Repeating Row Writes Tutorial

  --&CharacterID|[*S:character_id]
  --&RowCount|[*R:[&CharacterID]:repeating_npcaction:rowcount]

  --+|[c][b]Section Overview[/b][/c]

  --+Section|repeating_npcaction
  --+Number of Rows|[&RowCount]

  --?"[&RowCount]" -eq "0"|NoRows

  --/| Load the first Action and save everything needed for both tests.
  --Rfirst|[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction
  --&RowID|[*R:xxxActionIDxxxx]
  --&OriginalName|[*R:name]
  --&WritableNamePath|[*R>name]
  --&CompatibilityName|repeating_npcaction_[&RowID]_name

  --+|[c][b]Original Row[/b][/c]

  --+Action Name|[&OriginalName]
  --+Row ID|[&RowID]
  --+Compatibility Name|[&CompatibilityName]
  --+Writable Path|[&WritableNamePath]

  --+|[c][b]Method 1: Beacon !a Compatibility Write[/b][/c]

  --&ATestName|[&OriginalName] [!a Tutorial]

  --/| The familiar repeating attribute-style name is accepted by Beacon !a.
  --!a:[&CharacterID]|[&CompatibilityName]:[&ATestName]

  --Rbysectionid|[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction;[&RowID]
  --+Name After !a|[*R:name]

  --/| Restore the original name with the same compatibility route.
  --!a:[&CharacterID]|[&CompatibilityName]:[&OriginalName]

  --Rbysectionid|[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction;[&RowID]
  --+Name Restored|[*R:name]

  --+|[c][b]Method 2: Writable Target with Beacon !c[/b][/c]

  --/| Reload the row before asking for a fresh writable target.
  --&WritableNamePath|[*R>name]
  --&CTestName|[&OriginalName] [!c Tutorial]

  --!c:[&CharacterID]|[&WritableNamePath]:[&CTestName]

  --Rbysectionid|[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction;[&RowID]
  --+Name After !c|[*R:name]

  --/| Get the writable target again after the row refreshes, then restore it.
  --&WritableNamePath|[*R>name]
  --!c:[&CharacterID]|[&WritableNamePath]:[&OriginalName]

  --Rbysectionid|[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction;[&RowID]
  --+Final Name|[*R:name]

  --+|[c][b]Which Form Should I Use?[/b][/c]

  --+!a Compatibility|Useful when adapting existing scripts that already build repeating_section_ROWID_field names.
  --+R Writable Target + !c|Useful when you already have the row loaded and want ScriptCards to give you the safe Beacon path.

  --+|[c][b]Finished[/b][/c]

  --+Result|The same Action field was written through both Beacon repeating-write routes and restored.
  --X|

  --:NoRows|
  --+|[c][b]No Action Rows Found[/b][/c]
  --+Result|Select an NPC with at least one normal Action and run the tutorial again.
}}
